{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Let me go, I pray.</b> According to the Sages, of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah 1:29), who said that he was sworn by an oath to Yitro, he needed to entreat him to release him from the oath." "<b>And let me see whether my brothers are still alive.</b> And he did not disclose to him the matter of the mission, for HaShem did not say to him לֵאמֹר ('to say'), and they said in Torat Kohanim (Yoma 4a) that whenever He did not say to him לֵאמֹר, it falls under the prohibition of בַּל תֹּאמַר ('you shall not say')." "<b>Go in peace.</b> Meaning, he forgave him the oath. And all similar cases do not require formal release; rather, whenever the one who administered the oath forgives, there is no oath anymore."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:29.068606555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}